# Where the tarball beside this file came from. Update all three lines together on a bump,
# then re-run `make seed`.
#
# BUMP AT A MILESTONE, NOT AT EVERY TAG (ADR-0005). The app releases on its own cadence; gestion
# pins the version it decided to ship, so this file moves when a gestion release wants it to, not
# when the app tags.
#
# THIS ONE IS BUILT, NOT DOWNLOADED — it is our own app (ADR-0003), so there is no upstream release
# to fetch. `url=` names the tag it was built from rather than a download link, and the build is one
# command, run from the repo root:
#
#   git -C apps/estadistica archive --format=tar --prefix=estadistica/ v0.1.0 \
#     | gzip -n9 > provisioning/apps/estadistica/estadistica-0.1.0.tar.gz
#
# `--prefix=estadistica/` because ensure_vendored_app unpacks into custom_apps/ and Nextcloud needs
# the app id as the top directory. `gzip -n` keeps the mtime out of the header, so rebuilding the
# same tag yields the same bytes and the sha256 below stays checkable.
#
# TAG AFTER THE REBUILD, not before — js/ is committed and the bundle IS the deployment. The app's
# CI rebuilds js/ and fails on any diff; that arm ran green on 8c635f1, the commit v0.1.0 names.
#
# The tarball is code only (179 files, 754 KB). The REM figures are not in it: after install the
# app's RemJob downloads the DEIS window itself, ≈ 4.9 GB of database for the default 2023–2026.
#
# ONE tarball in this directory, ever: ensure_vendored_app globs *.tar.gz and fails on anything
# other than exactly one. A bump deletes the previous file, it does not sit beside it.
